      "id": "ch3-sec3",
      "num": "03",
      "title": "3. The range: there is no structure inside it",
      "summary": "Apart from bullish and bearish structure there is a consolidation period.",
      "figureId": "fig-ch3-3",
      "content": "Apart from bullish and bearish structure there is a consolidation period. Roman says it happens \"most of the time\" on the market: price cannot break out of the structure and just goes sideways. His key sentence: there is no structure within a range.\n\n### Why not?\n\nInside a range you can see a swing low and a swing high, but you have no breaks beyond the structure. Without a break there is nothing to confirm a trend, so there is no structure to speak of.\n\n### The beginner's trap\n\n### When you start drawing structure you will often be tempted to mark every little swing inside a range, hoping that a Break of Structure or a Change of Character is hiding in there. It is not. Roman's instruction\n\nFirst make sure you really are in a range.\n\nThen dismiss every break of structure that appears inside it.\n\nThe breaks inside a range are noise. Only a clean break out of the range counts.\n\n### Smart Money versus grid trading\n\nThe host joked that a range is \"good for grid bot trading but not so much for Smart Money trading\". Roman agreed. A sideways market suits one style and not the other, so know which one you are doing.\n\n### Example from a viewer (Dominic's chart)\n\n### A viewer posted a chart on Discord and Roman walked through it\n\nThere were swing highs at the top and swing lows below.\n\nPrice got stuck: it could not update those two swings in the normal way, because the previous swing was still where it was.\n\nSo price sat in a range for some time, and \"just a few days ago, about a week ago\" it broke out downwards.\n\nInside that area you do not look at swings. There is no structure in a range.\n\nRoman also promised a full stream about ranges later.\n\n### The range in a drawing\n\n> **Figure 3. Left: marking every swing inside a range. Right: draw a box, ignore the breaks inside, and wait for a clean break out.**",
