      "id": "ch3-sec9",
      "num": "09",
      "title": "9. Worked example 1: the SUI chart",
      "summary": "This is the best example in the lesson because it uses almost every idea so far.",
      "figureId": "fig-ch3-9",
      "content": "This is the best example in the lesson because it uses almost every idea so far. Follow it step by step.\n\nStep 1: an uptrend, then a scare\n\nSUI was in an uptrend. Then price broke below a swing low. Roman first called it \"actually a liquidity sweep\", then agreed that it could also be read as a CHoCH, because it was a confirmed swing low. Either way, price went straight back up, so the Change of Character was dismissed immediately: a fake CHoCH.\n\nStep 2: why the fake label helps\n\nIf you did not have the term, you would have to wait for another confirmation, and you would not be able to trade until price broke out beyond the old level. Because you can call it fake, the move up is just a BOS and you can look for an entry.\n\nStep 3: the entry\n\nThe setup looked like a decent risk to reward ratio.\n\nA fair value gap sat exactly inside the optimal trade entry area, and a liquidity sweep had happened below.\n\n### Roman checked the 15 minute chart. \"It was just perfect.\"\n\nYou would not enter on the first touch of the gap. You could enter \"somewhere here, after the candle closes\".\n\nThe result they pointed to was almost a 4 to 1 risk to reward. The host: \"We'll take those any day.\"\n\nStep 4: letting profits run? Be careful\n\n### The host suggested letting the profit run further. Roman agreed it is allowed but warned that on this chart the target was near the all-time high, which is very risky\n\n### Either price breaks through immediately, or\n\nyou get a cup and handle: price touches the area, pulls back (the \"handle\") to shake everybody out, and then pushes.\n\nThe host recognised it: the cup and the handle, which shakes out early profit takers and the stop losses of long positions. And that is what happened.\n\nStep 5: the all-time high reversal\n\nAt the all-time high area price made another push, a BOS confirming the uptrend. Then it printed a Change of Character and a Break of Structure below, confirming a bearish trend. After that BOS you could find an entry on the way down.\n\nStep 6: the rule and its exception\n\nRoman: as soon as you have a CHoCH, you cannot trade until you have the confirmation. Then he softened it: \"It's not a strict rule, because you can find some extra confirmations if you want.\" Those are the next section.\n\n### The SUI example in a drawing\n\n> **Figure 9. The SUI story in six numbered steps. This is a schematic made for study, not the real chart.**",
