      "figureId": "fig-ch3-10",
      "content": "At the SUI all-time high Roman stacked several signals so the trader could act without waiting for the confirming BOS.\n\nThe idea behind the table: you use a normal pattern (the flag) and the Smart Money reading (the swings, the CHoCH) to confirm each other. Roman: Smart Money Concepts \"collects a lot of knowledge from different strategies into one strategy\", so you can still use any other method you know.\n\n### The same trick on the way up\n\nLater Roman showed a Change of Character to the upside and pointed out a bullish RSI divergence just before it. You can almost see the CHoCH coming, and the divergence can \"sort of confirm\" it immediately. On the Bitcoin 4 hour chart a divergence also suggested that a move down was possibly a fake change of character, but Roman added \"we just need some confirmations\".\n\n### How many confirmations is enough?\n\n### Two warnings from the stream\n\nWhen three different strategies point the same way, the trade becomes lower risk, so why not take it?\n\nBut do not ask for too many confirmations, or you will never enter a trade.\n\nThe journal is again the answer: after a month, it shows which of your reasons were good decisions and which were bad. And both agree on the principle: keep the strategy as simple as possible, and execute to perfection.\n\n### Extra confirmations in a drawing\n\n> **Figure 10. Left: price makes a higher high while the RSI makes a lower high. Right: a flag or compression that gets taken out.**",
