      "content": "The end of the stream has two product announcements from the hosts' platform. They are summarised here so your notes are complete. Treat them as announcements by the presenters, and check the platform for current details.\n\n### The structure indicator\n\nA new indicator (called a smart money bot or swing high low indicator in the transcript) draws the market structure for you automatically, so you can scan markets and find good structures fast.\n\nIt was announced for release \"later this week\", in the Essential and Premium packages, not the Basic one. Anyone without it has to draw by hand.\n\nRoman had spent hours hand-marking a Cardano chart. They overlaid the indicator and it was \"pretty close\". The small differences were swings Roman skipped because he judged them not significant.\n\nAn algorithm follows rules: a breakout is confirmed, a high is a high. It cannot use human feel, and it cannot use the future (looking at five candles together while \"seeing the future\" doesn't work).\n\nThe advice: still learn to do it yourself, so you understand the strategy behind the indicator and can tell that it is drawing correctly.\n\nNext step they joked about: a scanner built on it.\n\n### The quiz puzzles\n\nThe platform is building a database of puzzles for different strategies (chart patterns, trend lines, Smart Money Concepts). You pick one and train your eyes. They were described as included for everyone, even the basic plan, and the puzzles are made without the swing indicator, so you do them manually.\n\nPuzzle 1. The chart showed a BOS above, then a CHoCH below, and a fair value gap. They said \"down\". The solution view showed the BOS, the fair value gap, and price entering the 0.5 area, which would have been a pretty good trade.\n\nPuzzle 2. It looked like a downtrend, but it was the hourly chart. Drawing the lines showed a bearish structure, then a CHoCH and a BOS to the upside, so it was now an uptrend. That gives the trading range, and the discount zone, so you look up. Inside that zone there was a small fair value gap followed by an order block. The answer was \"up\", and it was correct.\n\nThey stopped there to avoid spoilers. The current quiz was on premium and discount zones, with more to come on liquidity.\n\n### The community\n\nThe team has several traders, and invites outside traders who are strong in a niche topic to create their own quizzes, in exchange for free subscription time. They also invited people to join their Discord group to talk and learn together.\n\n### Quizzes in a drawing\n\n> **Figure 15. A six-step routine for any structure puzzle.**",
