      "figureId": "fig-ch3-16",
      "content": "Structure is read from candle body closes beyond swing points. Wicks are sweeps. Trends need a second break to be confirmed. Ranges have no structure.\n\n### Key terms\n\n### The rules in order\n\nDecide the state: bullish, bearish or range. In a range, dismiss every break inside it.\n\nIn a trend, only take trades in the direction of the latest BOSs.\n\nA body close against the trend is a CHoCH: pause, do not reverse blindly.\n\nA wick only is a sweep: structure is unchanged.\n\nWait for the second break, or for extra confirmations. If price instead makes a new extreme in the old direction, it was a fake CHoCH and you can trade the old trend.\n\nDraw the premium and discount zone on the trading range. Look for entries in the right half.\n\nA zone is not an entry. You still need a point of interest and a lower time frame pattern.\n\nBe patient about the entry. Prefer a candle close, avoid chasing, and skip trades under about 2.5 risk to reward.\n\nLog every trade, including the missed ones.\n\n> **Figure 16. What to do when price reaches a swing point: range, sweep, BOS, or CHoCH, and what each leads to.**\n\n### Common mistakes\n\nMarking every swing inside a range and hoping for a BOS.\n\nCalling a wick a Change of Character.\n\nTreating a CHoCH as a signal to reverse immediately.\n\nPlacing an order the moment price touches a Fibonacci zone.\n\nChasing a candle with a market order.\n\nPiling on so many confirmations that you never take a trade.\n\nGetting greedy with entry prices and not journaling the misses.\n\n### Checklist before any trade\n\n- [ ] State of the market named (bullish, bearish or range)\n- [ ] Last BOS or CHoCH marked, and confirmed or not\n- [ ] Any wicks through swings recognised as sweeps\n- [ ] Trading range and premium/discount zone drawn\n- [ ] A point of interest inside the zone\n- [ ] Lower time frame pattern or candle close seen\n- [ ] Risk to reward at least about 2.5\n- [ ] Higher time frame does not disagree\n- [ ] Reason written in the journal\n\n### Memory tricks\n\nBody breaks, wick sweeps.\n\nCHoCH is the knock, the second break is the door opening.\n\nRange = no structure, no breaks that count.\n\nZone is where to look, not where to click.\n\nMiss the trade, keep the money.\n\nEducational notes from the stream. Not financial advice: the teachers' figures and results are their own examples, and trading carries risk of loss.",
